15 0 obj
<< /A 54 0 R /Alt (Photograph showing a pepper plant greenhouse with a camera on a tripod labeled \215Collected scene.\216 Two close-up images on the right highlight distinct flower growth stages: one labeled \215semi-open flowers\216 and \215open flowers fully,\216 and the other labeled \215initial buds\216 and \215swollen buds.\216 Green arrows connect these flower stages to specific plants in the greenhouse, illustrating the sampling process.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 55 0 R /Alt (Diagram showing data augmentation techniques on a plant image. The initial image is in the center, with five variants around it: random rotation plus contrast, random brightness plus Gaussian noise, random translation, random rotation plus padding, and random occlusion plus pepper noise, each displaying subtle visual changes.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 37 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 56 0 R /Alt (Flowchart illustrating a leaf disease detection system: image collection in a field, data augmentation and annotation, model optimization, Jetson deployment with visualized code, performance metrics, heat map detection results under various conditions, and comparative visualization detection results for multiple models.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 38 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 57 0 R /Alt (Flowchart diagram of a plant image detection pipeline, including stages for image collection, data augmentation, annotation, model backbone, neck, and head architecture components, and output prediction with detected plant regions outlined in green.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 40 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 58 0 R /Alt (Diagram illustrating a neural network architecture with sequential blocks labeled Embedding, three FasterNet Blocks each followed by Merging, a final FasterNet Block, Global pool, CBS, and FC, connected by rightward arrows.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 40 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 59 0 R /Alt (Block diagram illustrating a sampling point generator for neural networks, showing data flow through various modules with labeled operations such as linear transformation, pixel shuffle, and network sampling, ending with a transformed data cube X prime.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 41 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
21 0 obj
<< /A 60 0 R /Alt (Two-part schematic compares neural network architectures: left panel \(a\) shows PANet with three feature levels \(P5, P4, P3\) and function blocks; right panel \(b\) shows BiMAFPN with hierarchical modules including BiSAF, RepHELAN blocks of sizes five by five, seven by seven, and nine by nine, and connections indicating feature aggregation and enhancement pathways for P5, P4, and P3.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 42 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
22 0 obj
<< /A 61 0 R /Alt (Comparison of object detection models applied to pepper plants under three conditions: occlusion, strong light with occlusion, and padding with shadow. Each column represents a different model\204RTDETR-r18, RTDETR-r34, RTDETR-r50, YOLOv8, YOLOv13, YOLO26, and CF-DETR\204showing variations in detection accuracy with bounding boxes and confidence scores marked in red or blue on the leaves.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 47 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
23 0 obj
<< /A 62 0 R /Alt (Grid of plant leaf images compares six object detection models\204RTDETR-r18, RTDETR-r34, RTDETR-r50, YOLOv8, YOLOv13, YOLO26, CF-DETR\204across blur, strong light, and shadow conditions, showing detection boxes and confidence scores.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 47 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
24 0 obj
<< /A 63 0 R /Alt (Normalized confusion matrix heatmap showing predicted versus true classes for CF, CB, and background. Highest values are 0.85 for CF-CF, 0.81 for CB-CB, and 0.80 for CF-background. Color bar indicates normalization from zero to 0.85.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 48 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
25 0 obj
<< /A 64 0 R /Alt (Comparison heatmap graphic shows four deep learning models \(RTDETR-r18, RTDETR-r18-Faster, RTDETR-r18-Faster-Dysample, CF-DETR\) under four conditions: strong light, shadow, blur, and occlusion. Heatmaps indicate model attention regions on leaf images for each condition and model.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 49 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
